In [[music theory]], an '''inversion''' is a rearrangement of the top-to-bottom elements in an [[Interval (music)|interval]], a [[Chord (music)|chord]], a [[melody]], or a group of [[contrapuntal]] lines of [[music]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Inversion {{!}} Jazz, Improvisation & Harmony {{!}} Britannica |url=https://www.britannica.com/art/inversion-music |access-date=2024-01-26 |website=www.britannica.com |language=en}}</ref> In each of these cases, "inversion" has a distinct but related meaning. The concept of inversion also plays an important role in [[set theory (music)|musical set theory]].

