'''Galaxy'''<ref name=":0">{{cite journal |last1=The Galaxy Community |date=20 May 2024 |title=The Galaxy platform for accessible, reproducible, and collaborative data analyses: 2024 update |journal=Nucleic Acids Research |volume=52 |issue=Web Server Issue |pages=W83–W94 |doi=10.1093/nar/gkae410 |pmc=11223835 |pmid=38769056 |doi-access=free}}</ref> is an [[Open source|open-source]] [[Scientific workflow system|scientific workflow]] system designed to make research accessible, reproducible, and transparent. Originally developed for computational biology, Galaxy has evolved into a domain-agnostic framework utilized across various scientific disciplines. Some examples include data science,<ref>{{Cite book |last1=Pireddu |first1=Luca |title=Proceedings of the 5th ACM Conference on Bioinformatics, Computational Biology, and Health Informatics |last2=Leo |first2=Simone |last3=Soranzo |first3=Nicola |last4=Zanetti |first4=Gianluigi |date=2014-09-20 |publisher=Association for Computing Machinery |isbn=978-1-4503-2894-4 |series=BCB '14 |location=New York, NY, USA |pages=184–191 |chapter=A Hadoop-Galaxy adapter for user-friendly and scalable data-intensive bioinformatics in Galaxy |doi=10.1145/2649387.2649429 |chapter-url=https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1145/2649387.2649429}}</ref> microbiology,<ref>{{cite bioRxiv |last1=Nasr |first1=Engy |title=microGalaxy: A gateway to tools, workflows, and training for reproducible and FAIR analysis of microbial data |date=2024-12-27 |biorxiv=10.1101/2024.12.23.629682 |last2=Amato |first2=Pierre |last3=Bhardwaj |first3=Anshu |last4=Blankenberg |first4=Daniel |last5=Brites |first5=Daniela |last6=Cumbo |first6=Fabio |last7=Do |first7=Katherine |last8=Ferrari |first8=Emanuele |last9=Griffin |first9=Timothy J.}}</ref> medical research,<ref>{{Cite journal |last1=Foschini |first1=Maria P. |last2=Morandi |first2=Luca |last3=Sanchez |first3=Alejandro M. |last4=Santoro |first4=Angela |last5=Mulè |first5=Antonino |last6=Zannoni |first6=Gian Franco |last7=Varga |first7=Zsuzsanna |last8=Moskovszky |first8=Linda |last9=Cucchi |first9=Maria C. |last10=Moelans |first10=Cathy B. |last11=Giove |first11=Gianluca |last12=van Diest |first12=Paul J. |last13=Masetti |first13=Riccardo |date=2020-06-17 |title=Methylation Profile of X-Chromosome–Related Genes in Male Breast Cancer |journal=Frontiers in Oncology |language=English |volume=10 |article-number=784 |doi=10.3389/fonc.2020.00784 |issn=2234-943X |pmc=7313421 |pmid=32626651 |doi-access=free}}</ref> neuroscience<ref>{{Cite journal |last1=Mitolo |first1=Micaela |last2=Zoli |first2=Matteo |last3=Testa |first3=Claudia |last4=Morandi |first4=Luca |last5=Rochat |first5=Magali Jane |last6=Zaccagna |first6=Fulvio |last7=Martinoni |first7=Matteo |last8=Santoro |first8=Francesca |last9=Asioli |first9=Sofia |last10=Badaloni |first10=Filippo |last11=Conti |first11=Alfredo |last12=Sturiale |first12=Carmelo |last13=Lodi |first13=Raffaele |last14=Mazzatenta |first14=Diego |last15=Tonon |first15=Caterina |date=2022-06-03 |title=Neuroplasticity Mechanisms in Frontal Brain Gliomas: A Preliminary Study |journal=Frontiers in Neurology |language=English |volume=13 |article-number=867048 |doi=10.3389/fneur.2022.867048 |issn=1664-2295 |pmc=9204970 |pmid=35720068 |doi-access=free}}</ref> and virology.<ref>{{Cite journal |last1=Lo |first1=Chien-Chi |last2=Shakya |first2=Migun |last3=Connor |first3=Ryan |last4=Davenport |first4=Karen |last5=Flynn |first5=Mark |last6=Gutiérrez |first6=Adán Myers y |last7=Hu |first7=Bin |last8=Li |first8=Po-E |last9=Jackson |first9=Elais Player |last10=Xu |first10=Yan |last11=Chain |first11=Patrick S G |date=2022-05-13 |title=EDGE COVID-19: a web platform to generate submission-ready genomes from SARS-CoV-2 sequencing efforts |url=https://academic.oup.com/bioinformatics/article/38/10/2700/6553662#394305808 |journal=Bioinformatics |volume=38 |issue=10 |pages=2700–2704 |doi=10.1093/bioinformatics/btac176 |issn=1367-4803 |pmc=9113274 |pmid=35561186}}</ref> 

Galaxy includes supports [[No-code development platform|code-free]] workflow development, GUI workflow visualization as well as [[command-line interface]] access, [[Job scheduler|scheduled jobs]], and cloud infrastructure management. It supports [[Digital preservation|data persistence and data publishing]] to facilitate collaboration, reaching a global community of over 750,000 registered users.<ref name=":0" />
